SYNTHESIS
================================================================================================================
A pressure search returning a DAG should be read as structure, not null output.

Pressure cycles/SCCs are the disproof-like signal: they say every runner in
a pressure core is blocking another runner in a closed dependency loop.
A pressure DAG says the opposite: dependency can be topologically sorted.
That order is a candidate proof certificate because it gives source and
sink peel layers that can be paired with endpoint-private rows.

The current hard LRC rows keep falling into the DAG regime.  That supports
a two-stage proof search:
  1. Build the mobile pressure DAG at a critical time or chamber.
  2. Peel along sink/source layers; if the endpoint incidence system cannot
     supply a matching private row, the obstruction must appear as a labelled
     pressure SCC.  The sampled rows do not show such an SCC.
